For any $g in G$, we have $g in g H$ since $e in H$, so the left cosets cover $G$. Conversely, every element of a left coset $g H$ lies in $G$.

If $g_1 H inter g_2 H != emptyset$, choose $k = g_1 h_1 = g_2 h_2$ with $h_1, h_2 in H$. Then $g_1 = g_2 h_2 h_1^(-1)$, so $g_1 in g_2 H$. For any $h in H$, $g_1 h = g_2 (h_1 h_1^(-1)) h in g_2 H$, hence $g_1 H subset.eq g_2 H$. Symmetry gives equality.
